<title>UK: UK'S Major declines comment on latest poll.</title>
<headline>UK'S Major declines comment on latest poll.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>British Prime Minister John Major on Wednesday declined to comment on a new opinion poll showing a dramatic reduction in the opposition Labour Party's lead to five points.</p>
<p>&quot;I've never commented on polls.&quot; Major told a news conference.</p>
<p>He said opinion polls were &quot;of no use&quot; in determining how his campaign was going.</p>
<p>&quot;I'm very happy at the way our campaign is going,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44-171-542-7947</p>
</text>
